  "name": "Two overlapping stelliums around the 20 December 2025 new Moon",
  "note": "Juno, Moon, Sun and Venus are pairwise within 8 degrees from 08:16 UT on 19 December, and Juno, Mars, Moon and Sun from 19:44 UT. Mars and Venus are about 10 degrees apart, so the five bodies form one conjunction component that is not a clique, and both stelliums are its maximal cliques. Each minute listed is a boundary T with T-1 and T+1: an edge is in T's registry when its bodies are within orb at T and T+1, because a leg's dissolving event marks its last minute in orb and the registry drops it then.",
